{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00621",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.93,
      "end_seconds": 12.25,
      "duration_seconds": 11.32,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor. I appreciate you fitting me in. My wife thinks I should have this looked at, so here I am. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.93,
      "end_seconds": 20.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.54,
      "text": "Happy to. Tell me, in your own words, what's been bothering you? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.45,
      "end_seconds": 32.06,
      "duration_seconds": 9.61,
      "text": "Well, I snore, apparently. Quite loudly. But the thing that actually worries me is that I fall asleep in meetings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.06,
      "end_seconds": 37.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "How often is that happening, the falling asleep?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.79,
      "end_seconds": 50.24,
      "duration_seconds": 10.45,
      "text": "Two or three times a week now. Last Thursday I nodded off while presenting the quarterly numbers. It was mortifying."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.96,
      "end_seconds": 61.36,
      "duration_seconds": 8.4,
      "text": "That sounds exhausting. And the snoring, does anyone say anything else about your nights?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.8,
      "end_seconds": 80.83,
      "duration_seconds": 17.03,
      "text": "My wife says I stop breathing for a few seconds and then gasp. She finds it frightening. I've been snoring for years, but it's worse the last six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.66,
      "end_seconds": 87.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Anything else you've noticed, mornings in particular?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.27,
      "end_seconds": 100.09,
      "duration_seconds": 9.82,
      "text": "Yes, I wake up with a dull headache most days. Morning headaches, right across the front, gone by lunchtime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.24,
      "end_seconds": 109.48,
      "duration_seconds": 7.24,
      "text": "Any chest pain, or pain in your chest when you walk up stairs?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.0,
      "end_seconds": 114.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "No chest pain, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.11,
      "end_seconds": 120.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "And any swelling in your legs by evening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.87,
      "end_seconds": 126.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "No swelling of the legs. My ankles are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.45,
      "end_seconds": 131.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Now, what medicines do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.01,
      "end_seconds": 148.92,
      "duration_seconds": 16.91,
      "text": "Lisinopril, 10 mg once a day, every morning without fail. Metformin 500 mg twice a day, although if I'm honest I skip the evening one when dinner runs late."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.9,
      "end_seconds": 163.86,
      "duration_seconds": 12.96,
      "text": "Okay, so the metformin is prescribed twice a day but some evenings it doesn't get taken. That's useful to know, thank you. Any allergies to medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.88,
      "end_seconds": 173.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "Sulfa drugs. I came out in hives once when I was given an antibiotic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.78,
      "end_seconds": 182.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.64,
      "text": "Noted. And your wider history, the diabetes, the blood pressure, anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.21,
      "end_seconds": 194.72,
      "duration_seconds": 10.51,
      "text": "Type 2 diabetes for about eight years, high blood pressure, and high cholesterol. They're managed, I believe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.18,
      "end_seconds": 198.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Any operations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.65,
      "end_seconds": 206.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "I had a knee replacement, the right one, in 2019."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.52,
      "end_seconds": 213.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Any sleep apnoea or diabetes in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.39,
      "end_seconds": 223.02,
      "duration_seconds": 8.63,
      "text": "My mother had diabetes. As far as I know there's no sleep trouble in the family."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.18,
      "end_seconds": 231.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "And what do you do for work, and do you drink?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.52,
      "end_seconds": 242.06,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "I'm an accountant. I'll have two beers on a Saturday, no more than that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.74,
      "end_seconds": 250.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "Thank you. Let me check your numbers. Your breathing, any cough or breathlessness, first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.2,
      "end_seconds": 255.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "No, my breathing's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.35,
      "end_seconds": 293.83,
      "duration_seconds": 17.48,
      "text": "Pulse 82, blood pressure 142 over 88, temperature 36.6, oxygen 96 percent, breathing 16 times a minute. You weigh 104 kilos and you're 178 centimetres, so your BMI is 32.8."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.72,
      "end_seconds": 299.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Is the blood pressure a problem? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.06,
      "end_seconds": 312.79,
      "duration_seconds": 11.73,
      "text": "It's a bit higher than I'd like, and I think the sleep issue may be part of it. Open wide for me, say ahh. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.3,
      "end_seconds": 317.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Ahh. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.73,
      "end_seconds": 345.13,
      "duration_seconds": 10.4,
      "text": "Your airway is narrow at the back of the throat, your lungs are clear, and your heart sounds are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.01,
      "end_seconds": 352.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "So what do you make of it all? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.28,
      "end_seconds": 366.43,
      "duration_seconds": 12.15,
      "text": "Given the snoring, the pauses your wife sees, the daytime sleepiness and the morning headaches, this fits best with obstructive sleep apnoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.43,
      "end_seconds": 372.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "I've read a bit about that. Is it dangerous? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.6,
      "end_seconds": 385.64,
      "duration_seconds": 12.04,
      "text": "Untreated it can raise blood pressure and strain the heart, and it's risky if you're drowsy at the wheel. That's why we should sort it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.61,
      "end_seconds": 390.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Understood. What happens next? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.57,
      "end_seconds": 403.91,
      "duration_seconds": 10.34,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a sleep study, which you do at home with a small monitor overnight."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 406.07,
      "end_seconds": 409.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "At home is convenient. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.39,
      "end_seconds": 421.58,
      "duration_seconds": 10.19,
      "text": "I'll also order blood tests, including your HbA1c and thyroid, and let's do an ECG here today to check your heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 423.24,
      "end_seconds": 427.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "All right. And in the meantime? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 429.76,
      "end_seconds": 439.34,
      "duration_seconds": 9.58,
      "text": "Avoid drinking in the evening, try sleeping on your side, and please don't drive when you feel drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 440.81,
      "end_seconds": 446.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "I'll be careful. How soon will I hear? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 449.36,
      "end_seconds": 458.09,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "Come back and see me in three weeks and we'll go through all the results together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 460.16,
      "end_seconds": 467.35,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "Three weeks. Thank you, doctor, I feel much better having a plan. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 470.06,
      "end_seconds": 473.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Good. See you then. ~"
    }
  ]
}
